### 🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch

<h3>Summary</h3><p>Please add a server-side configuration that can enforce structural and parameter-schema constraints for <code inline="">tool_choice="auto"</code>, even when clients do not explicitly send <code inline="">function.strict=true</code>.</p><p>A possible interface would be:</p><pre><code class="language-bash">VLLM_TOOL_STRICT_LEVEL=2 vllm serve ...
</code></pre><p>This would provide behavior similar to SGLang's <code inline="">SGLANG_TOOL_STRICT_LEVEL=2</code>.</p><h3>Current behavior</h3><p>In vLLM v0.25.0, structural-tag constraints are skipped for automatic tool choice unless at least one function explicitly contains <code inline="">strict: true</code>:</p><pre><code class="language-python">if tool_choice == "auto" and not _any_tool_strict(tools):
    return None
</code></pre><p>Source:</p><p><a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.25.0/vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py#L87-L112">https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.25.0/vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py#L87-L112</a></p><p>Therefore, a request such as:</p><pre><code class="language-json">{
  "tool_choice": "auto",
  "tools": [
    {
      "type": "function",
      "function": {
        "name": "get_weather",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "city": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": ["city"],
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre><p>does not use constrained decoding for tool calls because <code inline="">strict</code> was omitted. The model generates freely and the tool parser extracts tool calls from the generated text afterward.</p><p><code inline="">VLLM_ENFORCE_STRICT_TOOL_CALLING=true</code> does not change this behavior. It enables strict tool calling globally, but it does not treat tools without <code inline="">strict: true</code> as strict.</p><h3>Motivation</h3

